Required release obligations
----------------------------

1. MIT-style components require retaining the copyright, permission, and
   disclaimer text.
2. BSD-style components require reproducing the copyright, conditions, and
   disclaimer text in binary-distribution documentation, and prohibit using
   contributor names for endorsement without permission.
3. Apache-2.0 components require providing the Apache License, retaining
   copyright and attribution notices, reproducing any applicable NOTICE text,
   and marking modified files. No root NOTICE or COPYING file was present in
   the pinned module roots audited here, and soundconnect made no changes to
   those modules.
4. The root LICENSE files for klauspost/compress and sagernet/gvisor contain
   additional component-specific MIT/BSD/Apache blocks. Their complete
   upstream LICENSE files, not only this index, must be retained.
5. The release bundle must include the unchanged upstream license texts listed
   below in its documentation directory or equivalent “about licenses” view.
   This compact index records provenance and obligations; it is not a waiver
   of the text-reproduction requirements.
6. `sing-tun` and `sing` are GPL-3.0-or-later components introduced through
   the aTrust dependency graph. Their source and license terms must accompany
   a distributed corresponding-source release. AGPLv3 section 13 permits this
   combined work while retaining the GPL terms for those covered parts.

